  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TSP3 - Towards Safe, Protected, Productive, Peaceful Communities in Syria - Safe, Protected, Productive, Peaceful Communities (TSP3)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">TSP3 - Towards Safe, Protected, Productive, Peaceful Communities in Syria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Mercy Corps har l&#xe4;mnat ett projektf&#xf6;rslag till Sida avseende finansiering om 74 miljoner SEK under tv&#xe5; &#xe5;r f&#xf6;r genomf&#xf6;randet  av programmet &quot;Towards safe, Protected, Productive, Peaceful Communities in Syria (TSP 3)&quot;.

Programmets &#xf6;vergripande syfte &#xe4;r att st&#xe4;rka resiliens hos lokalsamh&#xe4;llen i Syrien genom st&#xf6;d inriktat p&#xe5; m&#xe4;nsklig s&#xe4;kerhet, st&#xe4;rkande av den lokala ekonomin samt konfliktf&#xf6;rebyggande aktiviteter. M&#xe5;len f&#xf6;r insatsen &#xe4;r att 1) tillhandah&#xe5;lla grundl&#xe4;ggande samh&#xe4;llstj&#xe4;nster i konfliktomr&#xe5;den; 2) &#xf6;kad m&#xe4;nsklig s&#xe4;kerhet f&#xf6;r ungdomar och kvinnor samt motverka negativa f&#xf6;rs&#xf6;rjningsstrategier; 3) utsatta m&#xe4;n och kvinnor f&#xe5;r &#xf6;kade f&#xf6;rs&#xf6;rjningsm&#xf6;jligheter genom insatser baserade p&#xe5; marknadsutveckling; 4) konflikdrabbade lokalsamh&#xe4;llen st&#xe4;rker relationer mellan grupper och individer; 5) B&#xe4;ttre koordination mellan NGO:er baserad p&#xe5; relevant och kvalitativ humanit&#xe4;r analys. 

Insatsen kommer beroende p&#xe5; kontexten att genomf&#xf6;ras direkt av Mercy Corps eller av lokala partners. Programmet kommer att genomf&#xf6;ras i olika omr&#xe5;den i Syrien och f&#xf6;rv&#xe4;ntas n&#xe5; 38.900 utsatta m&#xe4;nniskor varav 52% kvinnor och 48% m&#xe4;n, av vilka 50% &#xe4;r ungdomar och 10% personer med funktionsneds&#xe4;ttningar.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mercy Corps has applied to Sida for funding of 74 million SEK to implement the programme &quot;Towards safe, Protected, Productive, Peaceful Communities in Syria (TSP 3)&quot; during two years.

The goal of the intervention is to strengthen resilience of Syrian communities through a multi-sectoral approach. The objectives of the programme are to 1) Conflict-affected communities meet their basic needs; 2) Youth, women and most vulnerable are better protected and have a decreased use of negative coping strategies; 3) Vulnerable women and men have increased livelihood opportunities through market-driven interventions; 4) Conflict-affected communities (re)build inter-communal relationships; 5) Inter-agency NGO coordination mechanisms are enhanced through timely and quality humanitarian analysis. The intervention will, depending on the context, be implemented directly by Mercy Corps or by local partners. The programme wil be implemented in different part of Syria and is expected to reach 38,900 vulnerable persons of which 52% women and 48% men, of which 50% youth and 10% people with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Goal of the intervention is&#xa0;To strengthen resilience of Syrian communities through a multi-sectoral approach.
The Project Objectives are:
1) Conflict-affected communities meet their basic needs.
2) Youth, women, and most vulnerable are better protected and have a decreased use of negative coping mechanisms.
3) Vulnerable women and men have increased livelihood opportunities&#xa0;through market-driven interventions.
4) Conflict-affected communities (re)build inter-communal relationships.
5) Inter-agency NGO coordination mechanisms are enhanced through timely&#xa0;and quality humanitarian analysis.</narrative>
  </description>
